        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_af3e00bc14e94cb980e57af62c62c5ea",
      "statement": "Conversation binding resolves (tenant, adapter_kind, installation_id, external_actor_ref, external_conversation_ref) into canonical (UserId, ThreadId). Bindings are scoped by tenant and installation; pairing on one workspace does not authorize another.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/internal/reborn/contracts/conversation-binding.md#L68-L142",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b769898f1abfae77001513181d723804094c7003252623209bb3b68db6b50773:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8df4e240a0794ad6b00c37d898846e47",
      "statement": "Actor pairing resolves external actors to canonical UserIds through OAuth (Slack, Telegram) or operator configuration. Unpaired actors fail closed with BindingRequired; no message is accepted until pairing is established.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/internal/reborn/contracts/conversation-binding.md#L117-L127",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7929b9efcaa80219a51fa9f6002b50f382aab8b9023edf1064bf8d3b658c1d68:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_864a3e52a465419382c137370c2a94db",
      "statement": "Shared conversations (Slack channels, Telegram groups) create one conversation-keyed binding for routing and idempotency, but fresh ephemeral per-event threads keyed by external_event_id. Each inbound ping owns its own thread; redelivery replays that thread.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/internal/reborn/contracts/conversation-binding.md#L7-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44631f786656e286eda7952464c5d5f4a4b6e5e8d168179744aed1ee2f8ba713:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1a93624a180a479083782fdc1985b13c",
      "statement": "Shared conversation messages are admitted via fail-closed SharedConversationAdmission check: verified-ingress presence for the adapter's own installation. External channel membership alone is insufficient.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/internal/reborn/contracts/conversation-binding.md#L129-L130",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f418457ba505fba12385b302f48a5fa9671d31937365e8a532c349b2f971334a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fa794fbe461a4e03a2f1a313f27ea80b",
      "statement": "Outbound delivery resolution returns a single candidate target based on intent (LiveSourceRoute for inbound replies, RunScopedTarget for background notifications). There is no implicit fallback chain; the caller decides the target before resolution.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/internal/reborn/contracts/communication-delivery-resolution.md#L265-L298",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f8f27dcb73f8352b1bf845008920c05acac7799d690966a53c9b3530b7d86fb9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_21530911cd8947a495b54746c2961f0d",
      "statement": "Source binding and reply target binding refs are distinct. Source binding is the conversation route used for idempotency. Reply target binding is the exact external route (with per-message anchors) used to address the reply.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/internal/reborn/contracts/conversation-binding.md#L130-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e30e727b7ac4341de18984de34756aea49257271bf82014261712f322747a0c7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d874baddae83474bb10bb643ef0a2289",
      "statement": "SlackChannelAdapter implements ChannelIngress (parse Events API webhooks), ChannelDelivery (render to mrkdwn and post via chat.postMessage), and ReplySink (stream and message cadences for native threading).",
